# The words of parts that only existed in that build: found ones keep them, without a story. "id | item | name | text".
x2:a:aldo:2 | leather_leggings | The Worn-Through Knees | Aldo knelt in the snow in these to teach his granddaughter to chop, with the stone axe by the door, her standing on a stump so she could reach. Both knees are worn through. He said it was a good kind of worn.
x2:a:amberlight:4 | leather_leggings | The Cannonball's Tights | The Amberlight Circus fired its star act from a giant crossbow. These are the human cannonball's tights, singed at the back. The practice volunteer was a very surprised chicken. It did not get tights.
x2:a:apprentice:2 | iron_helmet | Practice Piece Two | "The visor's on crooked," said her master. "It's on at a jaunty angle," said Wenna. He laughed so hard he burned his beard on the forge. He kept the helmet. It keeps the rain off just fine.
x2:a:apprentice:3 | iron_boots | Practice Piece Three | Her first boots that the miners actually wanted to buy. She sold them for three emeralds and then followed the miner up the mountain to watch them work. He let her watch for an hour.
x2:a:apprentice:4 | iron_chestplate | Practice Piece Four | She hid her mark on the inside of the plate, a tiny bird, where nobody would look. Her master found it at once. He said nothing. He added his own mark next to hers, an even tinier bird.
x2:a:apprentice2:2 | leather_boots | Day 12 | Weeding the mandrake patch. Mistress says don't pull them up, they scream. I pulled one up. It screamed. I screamed and ran right out of a boot. Mistress screamed at both of us. Nobody is speaking to anyone.
x2:a:apprentice2:4 | leather_chestplate | Day 59 | Fishing for a frog with a crown on, for a spell. Caught three ordinary frogs and one very indignant prince, who was sick on my jerkin. Mistress says we'll "talk about the prince later".
x2:a:archercorps:4 | chainmail_leggings | Private Femur's Greaves | Private Femur once shot a creeper by accident and blew up his whole squad. These were all that came back of it. He was given a medal, a demotion and the greaves, in that order.
x2:a:archercorps:5 | chainmail_boots | Corporal Clatter's Boots | Clatter's arrows always went a bit to the left, so he stood a bit to the right. These boots are worn down on one side only. He has never hit anything. The Corps respects that.
x2:a:ashgrove:6 | leather_leggings | Waiting at the Gate | Back home, Ashgrove's village planted a garden for his return. It is still tended. Somebody comes at night and waters it, and leaves these by the gate. Nobody knows whose they are.
x2:a:ashmoor:3 | leather_helmet | The Judge's Hat | The fair judge had judged the contest for thirty years. At last he fired a bolt into the target between them and said: "For goodness' sake, just get married." They did. He wore this to the wedding. They argued about the rabbit.
x2:a:ashmoor:4 | leather_boots | The Daughter's Boots | Their daughter refused to learn the bow, out of spite, and became the best crossbow shot in the north. At the fair she beat both of them in one round. They have never been prouder or more annoyed.
x2:a:bandit:2 | copper_leggings | The Bridge-Keeper's Greaves | Her right hand, Big Tobble, held the bridge in these. Nobody crossed without paying the toll. The toll was a joke: if it was funny, you crossed for free. Tobble had no sense of humour.
x2:a:beekeeper:3 | leather_chestplate | Agnes's Smock | When raiders came to Honeyhollow, Agnes didn't fight. She put on this smock, walked out among them and opened the hives. The raiders left in a great hurry. Agnes wasn't stung once.
x2:a:bluecheese:2 | iron_helmet | The Inside Man's Helmet | The guard who let the thieves in was paid in cheese. He swore it was the best day of his life. It was also the last day of his job. They let him keep the helmet.
x2:a:bluecheese:4 | leather_leggings | The Rope Man's Trousers | He cut the rope too early. The cheese rolled down the mountain and through three villages, and he ran after it in these. It is still rolling, they say. So is he.
x2:a:bramble:2 | leather_chestplate | Bramble's Pit Jacket | Nobody knows what happened to his first shovel, or to the pocket of this jacket it was in. Bramble only ever said "the mountain kept it".
x2:a:breeze:2 | iron_chestplate | Toy Number Two | It used this chestplate as a sled down the copper stairs. Chestplates are not sleds. The breeze didn't know that. The breeze didn't know very much. It had a wonderful time.
x2:a:breeze:3 | iron_helmet | Toy Number Three | It tried to throw this the way the adventurers threw tridents. The helmet went into the wall and stayed there for six years. The breeze was very patient. It waited. It was worth it.
x2:a:butler:1 | chainmail_helmet | Chapter One: My Appointment | I entered the service of the mansion in my twenty-second year. The household was forty-one evokers, two hundred vindicators and one very old allay who did the dusting. I wore chain, as the staff were frequently attacked by the family.
x2:a:cartographer:5 | leather_leggings | Ilse's Wading Trousers | Ilse waded out to measure the depth of the sea, lowering a line until it stopped. One day it didn't stop. These came back, wet to the waist and no further.
x2:a:charred:2 | golden_helmet | The Helm of Varn | Here lieth the helm of Varn, who laughed the loudest, and was the first to go silent. The smoke hath blackened the gold. It remembereth his laugh, though he doth not.
x2:a:charred:3 | golden_chestplate | The Plate of Edda | Edda wore this, who had a daughter in the green lands above. She asked of each traveller whether the grass was still soft. None who came would answer. She asketh still, without a voice.
x2:a:charred:4 | golden_leggings | The Fourth Oath | The fourth never wanted to come. He swore because his brother swore. His brother fell on the first night. He hath stood at the gate ever since, guarding a promise that was never his.
x2:a:charred:5 | golden_boots | The Fifth Oath | Blackened, worn thin, and laced with a scrap of blue cloth. Blue was not a colour of the Nether. Someone brought it from home, and kept it, all this while.
x2:a:chef:2 | leather_boots | The Gardener's Clogs | Worn in the royal herb garden. The king never knew where the parsley came from. The gardener never told him; she liked the mystery.
x2:a:chef:5 | leather_chestplate | The Carver's Apron | Worn to carve the roast at the king's feast. The roast was a whole cow. The apron has never been the same, and neither has the cow.
x2:a:clocktower:3 | iron_chestplate | The Hour Plate | Beaten from the clock's hour hand after it fell. A line on the front still points at one o'clock, whichever way the wearer turns.
x2:a:crimsonbard:5 | golden_chestplate | The Bard's Last Costume | He wore it for his final show, on a stage by a lava lake. It is scorched all over in little swirls. Piglins say that's the dance. Piglins say he never stopped.
x2:a:crumb:3 | leather_chestplate | Crumb's Singed Vest | Tobias tried to light a cosy campfire once. The forest is still recovering. So are his eyebrows. So is this vest.
x2:a:crumb:4 | leather_leggings | Crumb's Lucky Trousers | He mined straight down in these, which everyone tells you never to do, and landed in a pile of diamonds. Then lava. Then, luckily, water. They have never quite dried.
x2:a:deepfisher:5 | leather_chestplate | The Daughter's Coat | She went down after him in this, against all advice. She came back up with his lamp, and a look on her face. She never fished again.
x2:a:deepspear:2 | leather_chestplate | Her Old Coat | Before the diamond spear, she wore this to swim out to the reef. She buried it on an island with a map, so that one day a child would find it and want to be a princess of the sea too.
x2:a:deepvein:2 | leather_chestplate | Memo No. 4 | Pinned inside a jacket: To all crews: the east wall is not to be mined further until further notice. Crew 3 is reminded that "it asked us to stop" is not an approved reason for leaving a shift early. Management.
x2:a:deepvein:3 | leather_boots | Memo No. 7 | Folded into a boot: To all crews: Crew 3's picks have been found. Crew 3 has not. The company thanks Crew 3 for its service. The east wall is to be bricked up by Friday. Management.
x2:a:diamondtools:2 | diamond_boots | Mira's Tunnel Boots | She dug a tunnel through the mountain in these, so the children of the far valley could get to school in winter. It took her nine years. The tunnel is still called Mira's Shortcut.
x2:a:diamondtools:3 | diamond_helmet | Mira's Helmet | She wore it cutting the beams for the tunnel, one by one, with a child's name carved into each: every child who'd walk through. There are two hundred and twelve names.
x2:a:digsite:2 | leather_chestplate | The Dunmarrow Jacket | Worn the day they dug the first trench at Dunmarrow, where the Old Builders' town lay under the dunes. The town was there. So was something else. The pockets still won't empty of sand.
x2:a:doctor:5 | leather_boots | The Doctor's Boots | When it was over, the valley planted a garden on the hill, a flower for every name with a tick. It is a very big garden. These boots walked every row of it, the first spring. Her cap hangs on the gate.
x2:a:embergulch:2 | golden_leggings | The Claim Jumper's Britches | Snake-Eye Pete jumped three claims that weren't his in these. Then the fourth claim jumped him. That's the gulch for you. It gives and it takes and it don't explain.
x2:a:embergulch:4 | golden_boots | The Gold Farmer's Boots | One fella tried to plant gold nuggets in the dirt to grow more gold. Walked the whole gulch in these, planting. Nothing grew. He's still waiting. Says it's a slow crop.
x2:a:ferryman:2 | leather_chestplate | The First Passenger's Cloak | The first passenger left this in the boat, very old and smelling of smoke. He said he wouldn't need it on the other side. The ferryman kept it. He keeps everything they leave.
x2:a:ferryman:3 | iron_helmet | The Soldier's Helmet | A soldier left this with a note: "for my son, if he ever comes this way, which I hope he won't for a long time". The ferryman has it ready. He hopes so too.
x2:a:firstchest:3 | leather_boots | The First Boots | And the first of us went down into the dark in these, with a pick of stone, and found coal, and made light, and understood that there would be no end to digging.
x2:a:firstchest:4 | leather_helmet | The First Hat | And the first of us built a house of planks, just big enough for one, and slept there the first night, and heard the moaning outside, and pulled this down over both ears, and was glad of the door.
x2:a:firstchest:5 | leather_chestplate | The First Coat | And the first of us met a cow, and from the cow came leather, and from the leather this coat, and lo, the nights were less cold. The cow was not consulted.
x2:a:firsttools:1 | leather_boots | Pip's First Boots | Pip was seven and mined her first block of stone in these, with a pickaxe she made all by herself, with only a little bit of help, which was mostly her dad doing it. She was a miner from that day on.
x2:a:firsttools:2 | leather_helmet | Pip's Sawdust Hat | She chopped her first tree in this. It took all afternoon. She came home covered in sawdust and said trees were "very rude" for being so hard. Then she went back for another.
x2:a:firsttools:3 | leather_chestplate | Pip's Digging Coat | At ten she made a stone pickaxe with no help at all and dug a cellar under the shed in this coat. Nobody knew until the shed sank a little.
x2:a:fishinglessons:2 | leather_boots | Mum's Boots | Mum cast like an arrow and reeled like a winch, standing in the shallows in these, and caught three fish while Grandad caught a nap. She never told him. She put her fish in his bucket so he'd wake up proud.
x2:a:flintkeepers:2 | leather_boots | The Keeper Who Stayed | One Keeper stopped in a village where an old man lived alone, and lit his fire, and stayed to talk, and left these by his door, and came back the next night, and the next, until the old man died warm.
x2:a:gardener:3 | iron_boots | The Watcher's Boots | Someone else's, left neatly beside the garden wall. The Warden walked past this garden for three hundred years and never once stepped on it. Nobody knows if it knew. Everybody hopes it did.
x2:a:gilded:2 | golden_leggings | The Collector's Greaves | Grashk's brute cousin collects his debts in these. The debt is still one gold ingot. The interest is now everything you own.
x2:a:glasswidow:2 | leather_chestplate | Mirelle's Apron | Mirelle dug soul sand from the edge of a portal in this apron, to make the window herself. The glass came out dark, and in it, sometimes, she could see him waving.
x2:a:goat:5 | leather_chestplate | The Farmer's Jerkin | The followers grew wheat to feed the Goat Prophet. He ate the wheat, the hoe's handle, the farmer's hat and one corner of this jerkin. The farmer called it a blessing. Through gritted teeth.
x2:a:goldsmith:2 | golden_boots | The Slippers for the Princess | The princess ordered golden slippers to dance once at her coronation. She danced once. Ferro had made them to last exactly one dance. They lasted exactly one dance.
x2:a:goldsmith:3 | golden_chestplate | The Plate That Fed No One | Ferro's apprentice asked him why. Ferro said a farmer worked his whole life in ugly clothes, and once, just once, he should wear something beautiful while he did it. He gave this to a farmer.
x2:a:grashk2:5 | golden_leggings | The Royal Guard's Greaves | Worn by the guard who shot at people who forgot to wear gold. He shot a great deal. Humans have very bad memories.
x2:a:greenhero:3 | leather_chestplate | The Green Tunic | He wore it into every dungeon. Every room had a switch, every switch a door, every door a key. He was very good at keys. He never said a word about it.
x2:a:hagra:2 | golden_helmet | Second Trade | "HELMET. HUMAN BOUGHT HELMET, HUMAN DROPPED HELMET IN LAVA, HAGRA FISHED HELMET OUT. ALMOST NEW. HOT. DO NOT PUT ON YET."
x2:a:hagra:3 | golden_chestplate | Third Trade | "LAST SHIRT. HAGRA HAS NO MORE SHIRTS. HAGRA HAS NEVER HAD SHIRTS. HAGRA FINDS SHIRTS. NOBODY ASKS WHERE. GOOD HUMAN. NO ASK."
x2:a:halvard:6 | iron_leggings | The Guard of the Last Wall | The Sunken Hall's last wall was a line of guards, standing shoulder to shoulder. These stood in the middle. The water came over the top, as water does.
x2:a:hollowfarm:4 | leather_leggings | The Fence-Mender's Trousers | Patched at both knees from mending the fences the cows had broken. The cows broke them again. It was a long, friendly war.
x2:a:lantern:3 | leather_chestplate | The Keeper's Coat | Maren cut the lighthouse beams herself one winter, alone, in this coat. The sea took the lighthouse anyway, but it took forty years and it had to try very hard.
x2:a:lantern:4 | leather_boots | The Keeper's Last Steps | Fished up near the spot where the lantern fell, still faintly warm, as if something down there is keeping it lit. They're Maren's. Maren went down to look for the light, and never came back up to say.
x2:a:lostlegion:5 | iron_chestplate | The Runner's Plate | Found with a note tucked inside: "Halt." The legion's runner had been carrying it the whole time. He was too polite to interrupt.
x2:a:mapson:4 | leather_helmet | Bram's Travelling Hat | He grew up on the road. He learned the bow, the sea, the stars. In time he could read a coastline like a letter. People started asking him about the shape of the coast.
x2:a:marrow:4 | iron_leggings | The Fourth Debt | Legs that would never tire. He used them once, to outrun the witch's crow, so she wouldn't see him leave. She saw.
x2:a:mire:3 | leather_chestplate | The Toad Garden Smock | Agatha grew mushrooms, warts and one lettuce, out of spite, in this smock. The lettuce is still alive. Nobody is allowed to eat it.
x2:a:mire:5 | leather_leggings | Agatha's Wishing Stockings | She waded into the mire in these, fishing for wishes. She caught three: one for a better cauldron, one for a cat, and one she kept in a jar. The jar is missing.
x2:a:moonfarmer:5 | leather_chestplate | Wick's Shed Coat | He wore it to build his shed, his fence and his small but deeply unsettling scarecrow army. The scarecrows wear the rest of his clothes.
x2:a:ninth:4 | leather_chestplate | The Bell-Ringer's Jerkin | The bell-ringer cut the rope after the ninth ring. It didn't help. The bell kept ringing with no rope at all. He ran in this. It still hums whenever a bell rings anywhere.
x2:a:ninth:5 | leather_leggings | The Last Harvest | The farmer of the Ninth Village knelt in the fields in these the day before. The crops still come up every spring, in perfect rows, for nobody.
x2:a:notdiamond:2 | diamond_boots | The Boots of More | With his diamonds he made boots, to walk faster to the mine, to find more diamonds, to make more boots. He forgot what the diamonds were for. He forgot to eat lunch.
x2:a:notdiamond:3 | diamond_helmet | The Helm of Alone | He made a helm and pulled it down over his ears, so he would not hear his friends calling him up for lunch. After a while they stopped calling. He showed his diamonds to his own reflection. It was not impressed.
x2:a:obsidianheart:5 | diamond_helmet | The Foreman's Helm | They buried the obsidian heart back where they found it, and the foreman set his helmet on top, like a gravestone. It's very quiet there now. Miners still won't dig within a mile.
x2:a:oldbuilders:3 | iron_leggings | Foundation Greaves | Dug up beneath a ruin older than the ruin above it. The Old Builders built on top of their own buildings, as if they were hiding the first ones.
x2:a:ostra:2 | golden_helmet | The Golden Hat | Ostra's husband brought back a hat of solid gold from his travels, completely useless for gardening. She wore it in the garden every day for forty years. Out of stubbornness and love, in about equal amounts.
x2:a:outpostledger:2 | leather_boots | Ledger, Page Two | Stuffed in a boot: Income: 1 allay (complaining). Expenses: 1 cage (allay escaped through the bars), 2 guards (fired), 1 cage (allay-proof, pending). Morale: low. Allay: thriving.
x2:a:outpostledger:4 | leather_helmet | Ledger, Final Page | Folded into a cap: Income: none. Expenses: entire outpost (a hero of the village was involved). Note for next quarter: build the outpost further from the village. Note two: much further.
x2:a:pell:3 | leather_leggings | Pell's Swamp Waders | Grandma Pell fishes in the swamp behind her cottage in these. She says she catches catfish. The catfish are not fish. The catfish are not cats.
x2:a:quiet:3 | leather_leggings | The Hunter's Leggings | A hunter fired an arrow into the quiet sky that winter, to see if anything was there. Something was. It sent the arrow back. These are his. There's a hole in them.
x2:a:ravagerrider:4 | leather_boots | Grimtusk's Farm Boots | When the raids stopped, Grimtusk and Petal moved to a farm by a village they'd once raided. The villagers were terrified for a year. Then Petal pulled their ploughs. Now they bring her apples.
x2:a:saltreach:2 | leather_boots | Little Pell's Boots | The youngest deckhand had never been to sea. He wore his brother's boots, too big, because he thought they would make him brave. They did. It didn't help. They came up on a line years later, still laced.
x2:a:saltreach:4 | leather_chestplate | The Bosun's Coat | The bosun lent this to every sailor who was homesick, because a warm coat is the same on every sea. He said it helps. Down there, he still holds it out to anyone passing by.
x2:a:saltreach:5 | leather_helmet | The Lookout's Hood | The lookout saw the reef too late. She has looked up at the surface every day since, as if she might see the next ship in time. Sometimes she does. Sometimes they listen.
x2:a:sculkchild:5 | leather_chestplate | Her Candle Coat | Her little coat, still smelling of candle wax. She said the Warden dreams about the surface. It wants to see the sun. That's why it's so angry about noise: it's trying to hear the birds.
x2:a:spearfisher:3 | leather_boots | The Teaching Boots | Every child at Kelp Point gets a stone spear first, so it doesn't matter if they throw it into the deep, and old boots, so it doesn't matter if they fall in after it. The fish build houses with the spears.
x2:a:spearmaidens:1 | leather_boots | Ninna's Boots | Hear now of the four sisters of the shallows, who fished with spears and feared no tide. The youngest, Ninna, waded in these, for she said a fisher should be as patient as the sea floor.
x2:a:spearmaidens:2 | copper_chestplate | Ada's Coat | The second, Ada, wore copper, which greeneth in the salt like weed upon a wreck. She said that a fisher should belong to the sea, and the sea should know its own.
x2:a:spearmaidens:3 | iron_helmet | Ylva's Helm | The third, Ylva, wore iron, and she alone of the four was ever wounded, guarding her sisters from the drowned on the night the moon went dark. She spoke of it to no one.
x2:a:stonesong:2 | leather_boots | Second Verse | Father built boats with his axe on the sand, the best boats in Saltmere, the best in the land; then the sea came up softly one night in the spring, and the boats were too slow for so big a thing.
x2:a:trialwardens:3 | iron_helmet | The Helmet of Hall Seven | "In Hall Seven, a bow that never missed! Except once! At the announcer! This is the announcer's helmet! THE ANNOUNCER IS FINE! THE ANNOUNCER WOULD LIKE TO MOVE ON!"
x2:a:trialwardens:4 | iron_leggings | The Runner-Up's Greaves | "The runner-up! Forty minutes against six spawners in these greaves! Lost on a technicality! The technicality was a slime! A standing ovation for the runner-up!"
x2:a:tridentkings:2 | golden_helmet | The Coral Crown | The second is the King of the Coral, bright and proud, who wanted the whole reef for a crown, and wore this. The reef is dying now, grey and quiet, and the King sits on it alone.
x2:a:twins:5 | leather_leggings | Fire Insurance | The twins once sold a village "fire insurance", then made very sure the village needed it. They ran in these. The knees are still scorched. They are no longer welcome on the coast.
x2:a:wellroot:2 | leather_boots | The Moat-Stepper's Boots | Upper Wellroot dug a moat to keep the Lower Wellrooters out. It was ankle-deep. Everybody stepped over it in boots like these. It was still a point of pride.
x2:a:wellroot:3 | iron_helmet | Lower Wellroot's Finest | The finest helmet in Lower Wellroot. It went to the Wellroot War exactly once, to the peace banquet, where it was used to serve the turnip soup.
x2:a:wellroot:5 | leather_chestplate | The Archer's Jerkin | The only archer in either village. He fought for both sides on alternate days, and wore this inside out on Tuesdays. He got paid twice. He's the only one who misses the war.
x2:a:whisperwood:2 | leather_helmet | The Dryad's Hood | Kett made it from the bark of the first tree he felled in the Whisperwood. It keeps the rain off. When the wind blows through it, you hear a sigh.
x2:a:whisperwood:3 | leather_chestplate | Kett's Hedging Coat | He wore it to trim the hedges round the Whisperwood, so nobody wandered in. One night, the hedges trimmed back. The tears in it are all leaf-shaped.
x2:a:woodcarver:2 | leather_chestplate | The Coat She Made Him | His wife made him a proper coat for their thirtieth anniversary. He never wore it. He said it was too nice. It hung by the fireplace next to her picture, and he carved beside it every night.
x2:a:wren:6 | leather_leggings | Holloway's Parrot Breeches | Her crew was all parrots, fished out of the air on a line. They perched on her knees to hear the orders. The breeches remember every one of them. Things were complicated on her ship.
x2:a:yrsa:1 | leather_helmet | The Outpost Cap | Yrsa grew up in the outpost, among people who took things from villages. On her tenth birthday her father gave her an axe and said "now you are one of us". She hid it under her bed, and this cap on top of it.
x2:a:yrsa:2 | leather_leggings | The Raid She Ran From | On her first raid she raised her crossbow at a farmer's boy her own age. He looked at her. She looked at him. She lowered it and ran into the forest in these, and she did not stop.
